WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.040
So, I just crossed the 100,000

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:06.400
subscribers. I've made about 60 videos.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.559
There's some things that I learned that

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.840
I know now that I wish I knew at the

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:11.360
beginning of starting this channel

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.880
because it would have saved me a lot of

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:14.160
mistakes. If you're trying to grow on

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.240
YouTube, trying to start a YouTube

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.000
channel, um, these are the seven things

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.000
that I want to share with you that would

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.320
be really helpful to me if I were

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.800
starting over now. Number one, make the

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.279
title and thumbnail first. Think about

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.560
getting your viewer to just click first.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:30.240
Getting their interest and getting them

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.160
to click. So that's the title and the

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.079
thumbnail. Then once you get the click,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.320
how are you going to follow that up? How

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:37.600
are you going to deliver exactly on what

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.239
they clicked and what they're expecting

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.320
to see? Once I started doing that, I saw

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:44.000
retention go up and clickthrough rate go

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.440
up. And then when that happens, when you

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.120
get the click and when you get people

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:48.800
watching longer, YouTube pushes your

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.160
video to more people and ultimately gets

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:51.520
more views. So I think that's the best

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.440
way to go about creating a video.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.440
Thumbnail and title first, then create

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.440
the video. Number two, [snorts] shorts

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.039
can actually hurt your channel. So, if

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.280
you look at my channel, I think I have

00:00:59.039 --> 00:01:03.520
one short up there. I don't do shorts. I

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:05.439
only do long form content. I have seen a

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:07.280
lot of channels that have gotten a ton

00:01:05.439 --> 00:01:08.799
of subscribers from shorts. Now, shorts

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.560
can get you a lot of subscribers. But

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:13.600
the problem is a lot of those shorts

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.040
viewers don't translate into long- form

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.720
content viewers. So, if you're just

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.479
going to be a shorts channel, great. Go

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.200
after shorts and post shorts. But if you

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:23.280
want to be a long form channel, be very

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.400
weary of the types of shorts that you

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:28.799
put out and if those viewers are going

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.880
to translate over into long- form views.

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:32.799
So when you put out a long form video,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.880
YouTube tests it first. They see how it

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:36.400
goes with your subscribers and then if

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.759
it goes well with your subscribers, they

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:41.280
push it out to more and more

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:43.360
nonsubscribers. If you have a large

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:45.040
subscriber base of people who just

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.880
subscribe to your shorts, but they're

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.880
not watching your long form content,

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:51.040
every piece of long form content you put

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.439
out is going to be harder and harder to

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:55.759
take off because your subscriber base

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:58.399
isn't watching that video. And YouTube

00:01:55.759 --> 00:01:59.680
assumes that it's not relevant, not a

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:02.479
quality video, and it's going to just

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.240
hurt your overall click-through rate,

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.479
hurt your overall watch time, and hurt

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.640
the overall performance of that video.

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:11.200
So, be very careful about the shorts

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.040
that you make and be strategic about how

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.959
you do it. You can still make shorts,

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.599
but the best way to go about it is to

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:19.040
make shorts that help your long form

00:02:17.599 --> 00:02:20.800
content. So, maybe they push people to

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.040
your long form content. Maybe your

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:25.920
shorts tease your long form content.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.440
Just make sure that they help each other

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.239
rather than hurt each other. Number

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:32.400
three, any video can blow up on YouTube.

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:34.319
Right now, their algorithm focuses on

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:36.239
quality content that people want to

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:38.879
watch. You don't have to have a ton of

00:02:36.239 --> 00:02:40.720
subscribers to have a video that gets

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:43.200
millions of views. One of my first

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.920
videos has over a million views now. One

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.560
of my other earlier videos has almost 3

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.480
million views. I made that when I had

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.760
just a few thousand subscribers. To do

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.160
that, just get people to click on your

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.080
video and then get them to watch it as

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.080
long as you can. If both of those things

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.680
hit, YouTube will just keep pushing your

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:01.360
video. And it doesn't matter how many

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.879
subscribers you have. So it could be

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.720
your first video, it could be your 10th

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:06.720
video, it could be your thousandth video

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.959
that blows up. But if you make a quality

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.239
video that people want to watch, doesn't

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:12.319
matter how many subscribers you have.

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:13.680
And that's what makes YouTube uh so

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:15.920
interesting to get into. It's such a

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.400
cool beginner friendly kind of platform.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.239
Number four is just be consistent. If

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.280
you make a video that's great, post it.

00:03:20.239 --> 00:03:23.760
If you make a video that you're maybe

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:25.840
not super excited about, still post it.

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.280
Be consistent. Get videos out,

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:29.360
especially in the beginning. Just

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:30.959
putting out consistent videos is going

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.480
to teach you so much. You're going to

00:03:30.959 --> 00:03:34.080
learn from the feedback in the comments,

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.040
you know, how each video does. You're

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.159
going to learn how to make better

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.840
thumbnails, how to get better

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:39.840
click-through rate. Every video look at

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.599
as a learning opportunity. Each video is

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:44.159
a chance for you to learn something from

00:03:41.599 --> 00:03:46.159
and build upon. And this is a process.

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:48.080
Just be consistent. The more videos you

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:50.640
put out, the more you're going to learn.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.879
Number five, try a bunch of stuff early

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.560
on. So, don't lock yourself into one

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:57.040
specific thing. You don't have a ton of

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:58.879
subscribers yet. um be the beginning is

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.560
the time to try out everything and try

00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:02.080
different styles of videos. Figure out,

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:03.599
you know, what gets traction, what you

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:05.120
enjoy making, what you think you could

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:06.480
make over and over again because you're

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.400
going to have to be making that content

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:10.159
for a long time. Once you have an

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.080
audience, it's going to be a lot harder

00:04:10.159 --> 00:04:14.239
to pivot to different content. If you

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.560
are a business channel and you start

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:17.919
making fitness content, people on your

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.680
business channel aren't going to want to

00:04:17.919 --> 00:04:21.600
watch your fitness content. Even if it's

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.360
extremely good, they didn't come there

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.440
for your fitness content. So, when you

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.960
post a fitness video and none of your

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.639
following watches it, then it's going to

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:30.240
be really hard for YouTube to push that

00:04:28.639 --> 00:04:32.320
out to the rest of the world because

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.080
it's not going to get past its your test

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.280
phase of your audience. So, at the

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.360
beginning is the time to test

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:39.199
everything. See what uh really clicks

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.800
with you and your audience and then you

00:04:39.199 --> 00:04:42.479
can go down a path because it's a lot

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.560
harder to pivot down the road than it is

00:04:42.479 --> 00:04:46.639
in the beginning. Number six is a very

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.360
important one and I learned this one the

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:51.040
hard way. Don't obsess over analytics. I

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:52.880
have tried to be a lot better about

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:55.759
YouTube analytics. Their analytics app

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:57.120
on the phone is like crack. Refreshing,

00:04:55.759 --> 00:04:58.560
refreshing, refreshing. They have all

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.919
the numbers going up. You know, how many

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:01.440
views you're getting every minute, how

00:04:59.919 --> 00:05:02.960
many views you're getting every hour,

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.800
how you're comparing to the day before,

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.240
hitting the dopamine sensors. I actually

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.240
started something where I just check

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.919
YouTube analytics once in the morning

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:12.800
every day to see how things are. Look at

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:14.160
a few comments, just kind of gauge where

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.520
things are that day, and then I won't

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:17.680
look at it till the next day. Don't get

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.280
into the trap of obsessively checking

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:21.120
your analytics. The YouTube app will

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:23.680
suck you in. Don't check analytics too

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:24.960
much. just do it once a day. And uh

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.360
that's worked really well for me.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:29.360
Lastly, number seven, think about, you

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.880
know, one type of person who you're

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:32.400
making your content for. Maybe it's

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.160
someone, a real person that you know in

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.919
real life, an avatar or somebody that

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:37.680
you're making your content for. And

00:05:35.919 --> 00:05:39.360
always remember that person every video

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:40.880
you make. Pretend like you're just

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.960
talking to that person because that's

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:44.560
your audience. Make something that you

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.720
care about and that you want to talk to

00:05:44.560 --> 00:05:48.960
that person about. YouTube is really

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:50.479
good at trying to make you chase views.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.720
The crazy thing is some of the most

00:05:50.479 --> 00:05:54.320
informative videos that I've made, some

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.759
of the most informative videos that I

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.520
know a lot of people make, don't get

00:05:55.759 --> 00:05:59.039
that many views. But the person that

00:05:57.520 --> 00:06:00.800
you're talking to, your core audience,

00:05:59.039 --> 00:06:02.720
the people who follow you, that's the

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.560
content that they really value. That's

00:06:02.720 --> 00:06:06.319
the content that they want to see. Make

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.840
content that you care about. Just keep

00:06:06.319 --> 00:06:09.440
consistently putting that out. You're

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.759
going to build an audience who values

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.199
what you talk about, the information

00:06:11.759 --> 00:06:15.120
that you're putting out for that one

00:06:13.199 --> 00:06:16.560
person that you want to talk to. And

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:18.720
that's going to guide you through all

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.240
the ups and downs. uh you know the good

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.759
views, the bad views. You're going to

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:23.520
remember why you're doing that, why

00:06:21.759 --> 00:06:25.680
you're making these videos and just

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.880
consistently make videos for that person

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:28.960
and that's going to connect with your

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.400
core audience. Yeah, I think that's

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.319
about it. So, those are the seven things

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:34.479
that I've learned from making about 60

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:36.319
videos and getting 100,000 plus

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:37.600
subscribers on YouTube. I wish I knew

00:06:36.319 --> 00:06:38.880
some of these things before I started. I

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:40.319
hope they can help you guys out if

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:41.759
you're going into YouTube going to start

00:06:40.319 --> 00:06:43.759
a YouTube channel. I hope they can help

00:06:41.759 --> 00:06:45.919
you avoid some of the same mistakes I

00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:47.280
made. Like anything, uh the best way to

00:06:45.919 --> 00:06:50.400
learn is to just start putting up

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:52.000
videos, start getting feedback, and uh

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.240
iterating. I'm still learning. I'm still

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.160
learning from every video I put out and

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.600
uh still reading the feedback and

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:59.440
seeing, you know, how I can make things

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:01.840
better. My ultimate goal is to just make

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:03.360
quality content that uh from everything

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.039
I've learned from business, from all the

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.960
businesses I've started, just pass it

00:07:05.039 --> 00:07:10.000
along to, you know, my audience out

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.199
there, my core avatar person who can get

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.639
some value from the stuff that I'm

00:07:11.199 --> 00:07:14.479
saying. Otherwise, I really appreciate

00:07:12.639 --> 00:07:16.000
you guys watching. Like and subscribe if

00:07:14.479 --> 00:07:18.319
you haven't already, and we'll see you

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.319
in the next

